  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Given the points $A(-2,2)$ and $B(-1,3)$, find the point $P$ on the graph of $y=2x$ for which $AP=BP$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p15-q15-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P\\left(\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p15-q15-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Write ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P=(x,2x)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and equate ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "AP^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "BP^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Since $P$ lies on $y=2x$, write $P=(x,2x)$. Using the distance formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}AP^2&=(x+2)^2+(2x-2)^2\\\\BP^2&=(x+1)^2+(2x-3)^2\\end{align*}$$\nBecause $AP=BP$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)^2+(2x-2)^2&=(x+1)^2+(2x-3)^2\\\\5x^2-4x+8&=5x^2-10x+10\\\\6x&=2\\\\x&=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2\\left(\\frac13\\right)\\\\y&=\\frac23\\end{align*}$$\nThus $P=\\left(\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 96
  },
